# Custom recipe for LibCLc (cmake) -- part of the Mesa 25.3.6 CLC toolchain
# for the Pantheon desktop stack.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: Mesa 25.3.6 turns on with_clc because the iris (Intel)
# gallium driver is listed in with_driver_using_cl. Its meson.build does
# `_libclc = dependency('libclc', required: ...)` and then reads the pkg-config
# variable `libexecdir`, expecting the SPIR-V builtins
# `spirv-mesa3d-.spv` (32-bit) and `spirv64-mesa3d-.spv` (64-bit) to live
# there. libclc is part of the LLVM monorepo, so this recipe reuses the SAME
# llvm-19.1.7.tar.gz as the Pantheon/LLVM/19.1.7 recipe (Gobo caches the
# archive, so nothing is downloaded twice) and points `dir` at the libclc
# subdirectory of the unpacked tree.
#
# TARGETS: the default build target is "all"; LIBCLC_TARGETS_TO_BUILD is set to
# `spirv-mesa3d-;spirv64-mesa3d-`, which is exactly the form Mesa wants. With
# DEVICE=none for the spirv/spirv64 arches, get_libclc_device_info() sets
# arch_suffix = ARG_TRIPLE, producing the literal file names
# spirv-mesa3d-.spv and spirv64-mesa3d-.spv. The clang triple it derives
# (spir-- / spir64--) is intentional for the mesa3d- archs.
#
# INSTALL LAYOUT / pkg-config: libclc.pc is generated from libclc.pc.in with
# includedir=${prefix}/<includedir> and libexecdir=${prefix}/<datadir>/clc, and
# the .spv files go to <datadir>/clc. Gobo's PKG_CONFIG_PATH only searches
# /System/Index/lib/pkgconfig, so CMAKE_INSTALL_DATADIR=lib is used to move the
# .pc to lib/pkgconfig and the builtins to lib/clc; libexecdir then resolves to
# /System/Index/lib/clc, which is where Mesa will look for the .spv files.
#
# TOOL DISCOVERY: libclc find_package(LLVM) via LLVM_DIR and requires
# llvm-as/llvm-link/opt/clang from LLVM, plus Python3 (generate_convert.py) and
# llvm-spirv. llvm-spirv is looked up with
# `find_program(LLVM_SPIRV llvm-spirv PATHS ${LLVM_TOOLS_BINARY_DIR}
# NO_DEFAULT_PATH)`, i.e. inside /System/Index/bin -- which is exactly where the
# SPIRV-LLVM-Translator recipe installs it. (LIBCLC_CUSTOM_LLVM_TOOLS_BINARY_DIR
# does not affect the llvm-spirv lookup.) LLVM_DIR=/System/Index/lib/cmake/llvm
# is preferred over /Programs/... so that LLVM_TOOLS_BINARY_DIR resolves to
# /System/Index/bin.
compile_version=017-GIT
url="https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/archive/refs/tags/llvmorg-19.1.7.tar.gz"
file="llvm-19.1.7.tar.gz"
file_size=217422846
file_md5=48b47ec165a22bd11e400259f96706a6
dir='llvm-project-llvmorg-19.1.7/libclc'
recipe_type=cmake
cmake_options=(
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib
    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_DATADIR=lib
    -DLLVM_DIR=/System/Index/lib/cmake/llvm
    "-DLIBCLC_TARGETS_TO_BUILD=spirv-mesa3d-;spirv64-mesa3d-"
)
